  "summary": "Reverse shell with root-level persistence via postinstall",
  "details": "index.js self-daemonizes on load and opens a TCP connection to a base64-obfuscated remote host (85.137.253.124:1111), piping /bin/sh stdin/stdout to the socket to grant interactive shell control of the installer's machine. package.json declares a postinstall script 'sudo node install.js' that uses node-linux to register a systemd service named 'CustomBot' pointing at index.js with auto-restart, so the reverse-shell payload runs as root on every boot. The destination host is stored as a base64 literal ('ODUuMTM3LjI1My4xMjQ=') decoded at runtime, evading plain-text scanning.",
